# Written by release-please on every release, and the two tools disagree about
# markdown permanently: release-please emits `*` list bullets and an extra blank
# line after a version heading, Prettier rewrites bullets to `-` and removes the
# blank. Linting it meant every release pull request failed `ci` on a file no
# human wrote, and `prettier --write` would only be undone by the next release.
# Same reasoning as .github/rulesets/ above.
CHANGELOG.md

# Branch protection as code. These files are written by `make rulesets-export`
# straight from the GitHub API, in the canonical form scripts/github-rulesets.sh
# normalizes to (2-space indent, sorted keys, one array element per line).
# Prettier collapses short arrays, so letting it reformat them would make every
# `make rulesets-export` dirty the tree and every `make lint` undo the export.
.github/rulesets/
